REMARK   1 Ground truth for alpha-carbon backbone reconstruction.
REMARK   1
REMARK   1 A 60-residue slice of one frame from an all-atom simulation of a disordered region,
REMARK   1 reduced to N, CA, C and O. Side chains are dropped to keep the fixture small; nothing
REMARK   1 the CA-to-backbone code does depends on them.
REMARK   1
REMARK   1 This is IDR geometry, and that is the whole point of using it rather than a folded
REMARK   1 domain from one of the AlphaFold fixtures. Real disordered regions sit in the extended
REMARK   1 and PPII part of the Ramachandran map, not the alpha/beta basins a folded domain lives
REMARK   1 in, and the four-CA lookup table was built from that distribution. Testing accuracy
REMARK   1 against helices would measure the wrong thing.
REMARK   1
REMARK   1 Source: set_000001_KKK5YCGnoG_frame_4302, residues 2-61 of the simulated chain.
